# nvn/textures: the Texture Memory Saver, DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP / DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_LEVELS, large compressed textures made without their finest mip level(s)
#
# Source:    https://github.com/cheemu21/kid-with-sword-remake  branch L, commits 17ede6aef90a60fbf0930a07babf3cfb7125d725 ("L7: the texture memory saver (DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP), from
#            the PRAGMATA investigation", 2026-11-17) and 2a18526087963e5afbdefb72ec27db49fe45851b ("compressed image textures are reduced too"); the first is ported from nxnative PR #1319
# Author:    patpat (the commits' name); the PRAGMATA investigation's patch is the original work of nxnative PR #1319's author
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds and contributors (nxnative LICENSE; the fork is MIT too); the attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m only)
#   A CPU-written compressed (BC / ASTC) 2D, 2D array, cube or cube array texture of at least DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP pixels on its shorter side (1 = 512) is made WITHOUT its k finest levels
#   (DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_LEVELS, 1 to 3, default 1; the fork's README sets 2) when pkg_upload_ builds it: the host texture's level l is the guest's level l + k. About a quarter of the memory
#   per skipped level pair of the largest level, and an area load converts, uploads (and on a GPU without BC, CPU-decodes: g_bc_cpu) a quarter of the bytes. Render targets and
#   uncompressed textures are never reduced. The finest level is about 3/4 of a texture's bytes. Translated: uploads (GPU gather, CPU deswizzle, and the BC CPU-decode branch of 0410/0411:
#   total_bc and the decode loop start at the guest level k, the blit goes to level l - k), views and sparse clamps (sparse_view, tex_level_shift), copies (lv_host: buffer-to-texture
#   still writes the guest level of the STORAGE, a copy of a level the host texture lacks is left out; a GPU texture-to-texture copy INTO such a texture does not write the storage back
#   and says so in the log, once per 1,000), CPU readback. The GPU direct upload and the partial re-upload (which counts guest levels) are off for such a texture.
#   Mac numbers from the fork (not ours): 2,300 of 2,329 large compressed textures of a walk are reduced; Metal memory 5.2-6.3 GB against 5.9-6.6 GB; longest frames 415 / 277 / 222 ms
#   against 2,678 / 526 / 487 ms; on an iPhone 18 Pro peak 5.8 -> 5.2 GB (fork, README: "under 5 GB") with frame generation on, frames dropped per 300 median 3 -> 1.
# DEFAULT: off. DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP unset, empty or 0 = every texture exactly as before (the fork turns it on for every iPhone through its launcher). Not read: its game profile / settings row.
# Price: close-up texture detail is softer (a texture at its finest mip level k=1 shows the next level, half resolution), mostly invisible on a phone screen; a texture the game copies INTO
#   on the GPU after creation keeps the guest's storage stale for the skipped level (logged).
# Adapted from the fork: hunks for the upload loops, tex_level_shift, tex_mtl_all (our tex_mtl_replay), the CPU readback and the BC CPU-decode branch (not in the fork's base) were re-made by hand;
#   the helper block sits before pkg_upload_ (its first user); a "2a18526" change (compressed IMAGE textures count) is folded into mip_skip().
# Shader chain: not touched (nvn_mtl.m is not in dmsh_chain.py's inventory; chain id b24b25240cad stays). A game's settings key is NOT used (none is added).
# Test: the fork's t_texture_quality was not ported. Checked: patch -p1 --forward --dry-run, no fuzz, in the series 0401..0415 + 0500..0505; nvn_mtl.m passes clang -fsyntax-only -fobjc-arc
#   with the host's include paths. NOT compiled to an object, NOT run, NOT run on a device. UNVERIFIED: a picture check on a reduced texture (mip bias, cube maps, array textures), the guest's
#   storage vs host level paths other than the ones listed (gsb_store, bcp_before/after, sparse placement textures for which sk is 0 because stamp is set only for pkg uploads).
# Use: DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP=1 and DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_LEVELS=1 (or 2) in app/profiles/0400486024DEC000.env.txt.

# REVISION 2 (2026-11-21, the review's M5, M6, M7; the saver stays OFF by default):
#   * M7 fixed: a texture with a compressed / uncompressed alias pair (bcp_find) is never reduced (the pair's block copies are made level for level and would copy guest level k to level 0).
#   * M6: a GPU copy FROM a level a reduced source lacks is still left out, but now said ([RED], once per 1,000): the destination's level stays undefined.
#   * M5 NOT fixed (a contained fix was not found: the storage of a reduced texture would need the levels it lacks): turning the saver on prints one [RED] line naming the known limits
#     (a GPU copy INTO a reduced texture leaves its storage stale and a later full re-upload brings stale levels back; M6; shifted levels for textureLod / texelFetch / textureSize; a
#     texture whose levels tex_desc cut is not recognized as reduced, L4). Use it only as an experiment (app/profiles keeps it commented).
#   Test: dm/gfx/tests t_mip_skip_limits (new), 9 checks, 0 failed: a 1024x1024 BC1 texture is reduced by one level alone, kept whole once an RGBA16F alias pair is registered, reduced
#   again when the pair goes; the [RED] limits line and the pair line are in the log.

# REVISION 3 (2026-11-21, review L4; the saver stays OFF by default, an experiment):
#   FIXED (contained): (a) tex_mip_skipped measured the host texture's levels against the DECLARED level count; a texture declaring more levels than its size holds (tex_desc cuts it, RED_ONCE
#     114) was therefore not recognized as reduced, and a copy of the guest's level-0 size went out of bounds: it now counts the levels tex_desc makes (tex_levels_made); (b) the
#     lazy reads of DM_NVN_TEX_MIP_SKIP / _LEVELS are dispatch_once (the first one logged twice if two threads met it). Test: t_mip_skip_limits, 18 checks (9 before).
#   NOT FIXED, documented here and in the [RED] line the saver prints when turned on:
#     * textureLod / texelFetch / textureSize in translated shaders see the host texture's levels, shifted by k against what the game asked: image-based-lighting cube maps, which are
#       sampled by explicit level, come out blurrier over the whole chain (a shader-side fix: the translator would add k to every explicit level; not contained, the shader chain would move);
#     * a render target or an sRGB / format twin view of a reduced texture (attach(), the view cache) is not checked for shifted levels: the saver reduces only compressed CPU-written
#       textures, which are not render targets, but a twin view made through tex_upgrade_pfv is sized from the host texture and was not tested;
#     * tex_level_shift answers 0 for a holder that is not an NvPkg (a texture the saver did not make): correct as long as only pkg uploads are reduced; not re-checked for others.
#     M5 / M6 (above) stand. Use it only as an experiment, behind a picture check.
